====================================================================================================
PART 2 -- THE PIN: which combination of (c0, q) does the jump fix?
====================================================================================================
  rho_d(r_b) mass run: d log10 rho_d(r_b)/d log10(M500/8e14) = q_jump = -0.343 +- 0.270 (Spearman -0.45, p = 0.14)
  the law's committed amplitude slope q = -0.414 +- 0.157 -> consistent within combined errors: YES
  rho_ph density slope at r_b: median -1.06 (= -2 + (1/2) d ln M_b/d ln r, the brief's '-1.7-ish')

  THE PINNED COMBINATION (algebra):
    jump: rho_ph(r_b)/rho_d(r_b) = A_b  =>  rho_d(r_b) = rho_ph(r_b)/A_b
    with rho_ph(r) = sqrt(G M_b(<r) a0)/(4 pi G r^2) (floor-A law):
    rho_d(r_b) = A_b^-1 sqrt(G a0)/(4 pi G) [M_b(<r_b)]^{1/2} r_b^-2
    -> the jump fixes, PER CLUSTER, the dust density at r_b; in the
       law's variables rho_d(r) ~ 10^{c0} (M500/8e14)^q (r/R500)^-0.99
       this pins the ONE linear combination
       c0 + q log10(M500/8e14) = log10[rho_d(r_b) (r_b/R500)^{-0.99}],
       i.e. the c0-direction at r_b -- leaving the perpendicular
       direction (the mass slope q's own value) EMPIRICAL unless the
       mass run of rho_ph(r_b) pins it (q_jump above).

====================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE FULL DERIVATION STATUS: (c0, q) = DERIVED / 1-PARAM / 2-PARAM
====================================================================================================
  G182 (dispatched per WAVEBOARD 'radial dispersion at the cap (G182
  dispatched)' -- NOT on disk at lane time) closes sigma_d(r_b), the
  infall dispersion at the cap = G159 V3's named missing piece:
    G159:  A_b = (sigma_ph / sigma_d(r_b))^3   [dressed jump, p = 3]
    G182:  sigma_d(r_b) EXACT  ->  A_b a SINGLE number (band collapses)
    jump:  rho_d(r_b) = rho_ph(r_b)/A_b  ->  c0-direction pinned:
           c0 = log10[rho_ph(r_b) (r_b/R500)^{0.99} / A_b] - q log10(M500/8e14)
    q direction: the mass run of rho_ph(r_b) (Part 2, q_jump).
  STATUS with today's committed data: ONE-PARAMETER EMPIRICAL + consistency: the jump pins the c0-combination (median R = 1.09, 12/12 inside the derived band); q's mass dimension remains MEASURED (-0.414 +- 0.157), CONSISTENT with the derived mass run (q_jump = -0.34 +- 0.27, within combined errors) but not independently derived (12-point power)
  -> G182 landing collapses the A_b band to one number and turns the
     c0-direction into a COMPUTED number; the LAST cluster freedom is
     then at most the single number q.

